Machine Learning Based Intrusion Detection System (IDS)

1. Abstract
A Machine Learning Based Intrusion Detection System (IDS) is a cybersecurity system used to identify suspicious activities in a computer network. It uses machine learning algorithms to classify network traffic as normal or suspicious. In this project, the Random Forest algorithm is used to analyze network traffic features and detect possible attacks. The system trains a model using labelled data and evaluates its performance using accuracy, precision, recall and F1-score. This project demonstrates how machine learning can help improve network security.
2. Introduction
An Intrusion Detection System monitors network activities to identify unauthorized access, suspicious connections and possible cyberattacks.
Traditional IDS systems mainly use predefined rules or signatures. Machine learning-based IDS can learn patterns from labelled data and classify new records.
The proposed project uses Python and the Random Forest algorithm to demonstrate network intrusion detection.
3. Problem Statement
Traditional intrusion detection systems may fail to identify unfamiliar attack patterns. Therefore, a machine learning-based system is proposed to classify network traffic and identify potentially suspicious activities.
4. Objectives
To understand the concept of intrusion detection.
To develop an IDS using machine learning.
To classify network traffic into normal and suspicious categories.
To implement the Random Forest algorithm.
To evaluate model performance using standard metrics.
To improve understanding of machine learning applications in cybersecurity.
5. Proposed Methodology
The project follows these steps:
Data collection: Obtain labelled network traffic data or use synthetic demonstration data.
Data preprocessing: Clean the data and select relevant features.
Data splitting: Divide the dataset into training and testing sets.
Model training: Train the Random Forest classifier.
Prediction: Classify test records as normal or suspicious.
Evaluation: Calculate accuracy, precision, recall and F1-score.
Result analysis: Review the results and identify limitation
