11. Results and Discussion
The program trains the Random Forest classifier and predicts labels for the test dataset. It displays the accuracy and classification report.
The evaluation metrics are:
*Accuracy: Overall proportion of correct predictions.
*Precision: How many records predicted as attacks are actually attacks, according to the test labels.
*Recall: How many actual attack-labelled records the model identifies.
*F1-score:A combined measure of precision and recall. 

The actual scores should be recorded after running the program. Results from synthetic data do not demonstrate real-world network detection performance. 

